<h1>Maggie Trevor</h1>
<p>Cook County Commissioner, 9th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Democratic. Incumbent.</p>
<p><a href="https://maggietrevor4cook.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (maggietrevor4cook.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Her campaign site lists access to health care, stewardship of the environment and forest preserves, transportation improvements, and equitable taxes with efficient use of tax dollars as her priorities. Her re-election statement says federal changes to Medicaid and the ACA, public transit funding, and the EPA will strain county health services, transit projects, and local environmental protections, and calls for fiscal responsibility and better coordination of county services.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>University of Chicago PhD in political science who taught at the University of Iowa, then spent two decades as a health care market researcher (Kaiser Foundation Health Plan, Blue Shield of California, vice president of YouGov Healthcare) before founding Trevor Research Services in Rolling Meadows in 2014.</p>
